<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Embattled new White House Press Secretary Zacharia 'let go' from her role</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:338f22e50acf194d18b98621691c3d8c9d48bf2c2d5deb06ec8b639572856a73</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:57:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261016-embattled-new-white-house-press-secretary-zacharia-let-go-from-her-role" /><summary type="html">A White House Press official said Friday that Secretary ​Katie Zacharia was "let go" from her role after US President Donald Trump signaled she was on her way out, a week after he picked her for the post. Zacharia's credentials as an attorney had come under scrutiny and she admitted to not having passed the bar in an interview with Fox News on Thursday.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Thanks a lot, Trump': Wyoming conservatives divided ahead of US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9dacb166367f6ef2e8f1249ccde83861a76f64c8460b8e9cb37cb233c413272b</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T12:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261016-thanks-a-lot-trump-wyoming-conservatives-divided-ahead-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">Famous for its cowboy culture, Wyoming is the least populated, the most rural and the most conservative of all the US states. With two weeks to go until the midterm elections, our reporters James André and Sylvain Rousseau travelled across this Republican stronghold and found that the party of US President Donald Trump is deeply divided in the Cowboy State.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>No, this oil tanker didn’t carry Russian diesel to the United States</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f62b46b2c59fcc9e161288aeb6c7e362808b0c519efde763ca58ef90876f7457</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T08:36:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261016-oil-tanker-carry-russian-diesel-united-states" /><summary type="html">Following US President Donald Trump's October 9 announcement of an agreement signed with Russian President Vladimir Putin to import Russian diesel into the United States, a number of pro-Russian social media accounts began claiming that a Russian oil tanker was already carrying thousands of barrels of diesel to the United States. The ship was actually carrying fertiliser.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Teen shooter kills three children and teacher at Oregon elementary school</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49c3b2cea4705a2bfaedea05514bd85f40d54d9a123531c0f287be1239cb9aa2</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T21:58:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-two-hospitalised-after-shooting-at-oregon-elementary-school-gunman-dead--5a6aa5ab65a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-two-hospitalised-after-shooting-at-oregon-elementary-school-gunman-dead" /><summary type="html">A 16-year-old gunman killed three children and a teacher at Silver Rail Elementary School in Bend, Oregon, on Thursday before being killed by a community member who pursued him inside, police said. Two other people were wounded in the shooting.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Fake AI images of protester go viral after woman punched at Trump's Ohio rally</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de25d7cd656b0a41faecc815209ded1a7719593baaf354ee88f65419b488a30d</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T19:47:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/fake-ai-images-of-protester-go-viral-after-woman-punched-at-trump-s-ohio-rally--84322c184e38.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/fake-ai-images-of-protester-go-viral-after-woman-punched-at-trump-s-ohio-rally" /><summary type="html">A protester who heckled US President Donald Trump at his midterm rally in Youngstown, Ohio, was physically assaulted and removed from the event, but fake AI-generated photos recreating the incident are going viral online. The images carry digital watermarks identifying them as AI-generated. While footage confirms the woman was punched, there is no evidence to support Trump's claim that the protester was "paid" to disrupt his speech, as he mocked her weight. Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuela's Nicolas Maduro and wife Cilia Flores deny US torture charges as 'false accusations'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33c98fe8f032db65ce1876f8f66c0f2c952bb7a9dec6603cf9b0ad6f41ae33be</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T18:11:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-venezuela-s-nicolas-maduro-and-wife-cilia-flores-deny-us-torture-charges-as-false-accusatio--a2d0e0fa417a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-venezuela-s-nicolas-maduro-and-wife-cilia-flores-deny-us-torture-charges-as-false-accusations" /><summary type="html">Ousted Venezuelan president Nicolas Maduro and his wife Cilia Flores pleaded not guilty on Thursday to new torture charges brought against them by US authorities, calling them “false allegations". The couple has been held in a New York jail since their capture in early January and is facing a new indictment accusing them of conspiring to torture political opponents and US citizens.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'We're done': Ukraine resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries as 'only leverage' for peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b7522612baac49fa380a52e22411a4ed1bf64b87ec4748be39734e34c0d0010</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T16:14:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-we-re-done-ukraine-resumes-strikes-on-russian-oil-refineries-as-only-leverage-for-peace-tal--b4d9641c071b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-we-re-done-ukraine-resumes-strikes-on-russian-oil-refineries-as-only-leverage-for-peace-talks-1" /><summary type="html">Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. As Zelensky declares Ukraine "done" with Trump's self-declared energy ceasefire and resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries, Zalmayev warns: "When you talk about the energy ceasefire, it presupposes two to be able to tango and to dance this dance." He challenges the legitimacy of Trump's unilateral announcement, made without agreement between Moscow and Kyiv, as Russia continues attacking Ukraine's energy infrastructure. Yet he cautions that Zelensky may need tactical restraint to preserve vital US support. Zalmayev also examines Western sanctions, frozen Russian assets, and Washington's pursuit of economic normalization with Moscow without meaningful Russian concessions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Midterms 2026: Georgia's Ossof-Collins showdown lies at the heart of the battle for US Senate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7e55ee4849c9ddba60cff8c7df0e0039ab2d8669ab41ccaf65543b5bdebb6d1</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T15:14:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-2026-midterms-georgia-s-ossof-collins-showdown-lies-at-the-heart-of-the-battle-for-us-senat--052a42259b79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-2026-midterms-georgia-s-ossof-collins-showdown-lies-at-the-heart-of-the-battle-for-us-senate" /><summary type="html">In Georgia, Democrat Jon Ossoff’s seat is one of the key contests in the US mid-term elections on 3 November. In this state, which was won by Donald Trump in 2024, the incumbent senator is facing Republican Mike Collins. Our reporter Leela Jacinto visited Manuel’s Tavern, a historic bar in Atlanta that has been frequented for decades by Democratic politicians. There, patrons watched the debate between the two candidates.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump cancels livestreaming of Fort Hood shooter’s firing squad execution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:728849932b9c6ae2fc47ca551c774b38130833ba7e40874ec93848f1b0820978</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:58:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-fort-hood-shooter-s-firing-squad-execution-will-not-be-livestreamed-trump-says--e314adab8cb1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-fort-hood-shooter-s-firing-squad-execution-will-not-be-livestreamed-trump-says" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Thursday that he was cancelling plans to livestream the firing squad execution of a convicted military base shooter – a project that had sparked outrage in the United States. Nidal Hasan is scheduled to be executed on December 3 at Fort Hood in Texas, where he killed 13 people in 2009.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Haiti: Capoeira classes aim to promote peace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7465153e4b87eff7cdccd3b13bce28d5226ff97011637c78595965b5940aa0d</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T14:25:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261015-haiti-capoeira-classes-promote-peace--3eb12a28ea75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261015-haiti-capoeira-classes-promote-peace" /><summary type="html">An association in Haiti is organising capoeira classes – an Afro-Brazilian martial art – in an attempt to reduce community violence and promote social reintegration. The Observers team spoke to its founder, Rodney Jean Marc, who said their doors are open to everyone, “even children in armed gangs”. The initiative takes place as the country's security situation has worsened in recent years.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands of Colombians march against new right-wing president's policies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b4bb8d9022136cfdfffdb389e267bfe66d7702af3d986df37c53f9ab6ece80a</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T01:57:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-thousands-protest-colombia-right-wing-president--3e6c97bc299e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-thousands-protest-colombia-right-wing-president" /><summary type="html">Thousands of Colombians protested peacefully across the country on Wednesday against right-wing President Abelardo de la Espriella, in the opposition’s first major demonstrations since he took office in August. Former leftist president Gustavo Petro led a rally in Bogota joined by trade unionists, Indigenous groups, students and feminist activists.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Lula's party to file complaint against Meta over Brazil election interference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7070d33514fed55d43d8c046903eb99b78bf80a2c2bb7396426a1a5cc08307b4</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T23:52:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-lula-party-meta-election-interference-brazil-runoff--db9710e4afed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-lula-party-meta-election-interference-brazil-runoff" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva’s party plans to file a complaint against Meta with the Organisation of American States alleging election interference, his campaign said Wednesday. The party accuses Meta of restricting Lula’s online content ahead of the October 25 presidential runoff against far-right Senator Flavio Bolsonaro. Meta denies the allegations.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Musk says Zelensky should 'go' as doubts grow over US support for Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9d244f5c0a61b77b9c93694a3bfdfcda54eb7c5e64e8161b60f48b44d726ecd</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T20:19:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-musk-says-us-govt-responsible-for-any-starshield-restrictions-affecting-ukraine--9dec4e505e36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-musk-says-us-govt-responsible-for-any-starshield-restrictions-affecting-ukraine" /><summary type="html">SpaceX CEO Elon Musk on Wednesday called on Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky to "go" after Kyiv raised doubts over US support for his country against the Russian invasion. A day earlier, Musk said any restrictions on Ukraine's use of the Starshield system would be due to decisions made by the US government after Zelensky called on Musk to restore Starlink, which Kyiv says has been slowed down.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump sparks outrage over AI tiger video after sharing footage of fatal UK attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f002ebea7d466b68044d7054c42fdcd14eeb9af132de4d9c89fa5c4169fe338</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T19:39:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-sparks-outrage-over-ai-tiger-video-after-sharing-footage-of-fatal-uk-attack-1--f6bcc553bc17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-sparks-outrage-over-ai-tiger-video-after-sharing-footage-of-fatal-uk-attack-1" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump has sparked outrage after sharing the distressing footage of a 23-year-old man with mental illness being fatally mauled by a tiger at Yorkshire Wildlife Park in the UK, captioned "Don't ever mess with nature!" This was followed hours later by an AI-generated video of himself taming a tiger. The posts have been condemned as disrespectful to the victim and his grieving family, who have urged people to stop sharing harrowing content of the attack. Vedika Bahl tells us more.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>In Phoenix, young ultra-conservatives look to carry on Charlie Kirk’s legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4ebb697506c3a97fe8724a88d883fb458cd70edb184b30c4df738736f4fae75</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T14:37:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-in-phoenix-young-ultra-conservatives-look-to-carry-on-charlie-kirk-s-legacy--b1cd212fca53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-in-phoenix-young-ultra-conservatives-look-to-carry-on-charlie-kirk-s-legacy" /><summary type="html">More than a year after the assassination of far-right influencer Charlie Kirk in September 2025, young activists from the organisation he co-founded, Turning Point USA, are working tirelessly to honour his legacy by rallying the youth vote ahead of the US midterm elections.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump's crackdown on migrants: New documentary investigates ICE operations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d75d3a7b9bab3f20b93b6a8c6266f148dbdd61f47221e0729dca080d7ec19db</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T11:51:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261014-trump-s-crackdown-on-migrants-new-documentary-investigates-ice-operations--9b8e9754fee1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261014-trump-s-crackdown-on-migrants-new-documentary-investigates-ice-operations" /><summary type="html">A new documentary from our sister channel France Télévisions explores US President Donald Trump's relentless crackdown on immigration and the agency carrying it out – United States Immigration and Customs Enforcement, better known as ICE. "ICE : La chasse a l'homme", or "A Manhunt Named ICE" interviews agents and also some of the people who lives have been turned upside down by ICE operations. In Perspective, we spoke to the film's co-writer Marine Pradel.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Trump asks US ambassador to Greece Kimberly Guilfoyle to resign over bribery allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb1fd2e472d25417b1ee416761b1130989e7529e969ad891e068ff9df5094e55</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T03:23:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-trump-asks-us-ambassador-to-greece-kimberly-guilfoyle-to-resign-over-allegations--7d7bb6aaf516.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-trump-asks-us-ambassador-to-greece-kimberly-guilfoyle-to-resign-over-allegations" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump asked his ambassador to Greece Kimberly Guilfoyle to resign on Tuesday after reports alleged she sought $100,000 from a Trump supporter to pay personal credit card debt and accepted luxury trips and hotel stays from wealthy Greek businessmen. Guilfoyle denied wrongdoing and vowed to defend her reputation.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>FBI arrests Saudi OpenAI employee for allegedly bugging San Francisco office</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d057919e7ce811b31a603b19da067e7266424008278b94b3bcf0ddaeb5b9e5f</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T23:49:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-fbi-arrests-saudi-openai-employee-for-allegedly-bugging-san-francisco-office--3d35fd945b9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-fbi-arrests-saudi-openai-employee-for-allegedly-bugging-san-francisco-office" /><summary type="html">The FBI said on Wednesday it has arrested a Saudi national employed as an engineer at OpenAI on suspicions that he had bugged a conference room at the company's San Francisco office with a "sophisticated recording device".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump asks Greece ambassador to resign amid ethics scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2ba366ea4a7211381dd24a81ba330ccb26b0e0ab0288e204b0082419565de7c</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:29:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-asks-greece-ambassador-to-resign-amid-ethics-scandal--24c18b5f16df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-asks-greece-ambassador-to-resign-amid-ethics-scandal" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's administration has asked his ambassador to Greece Kimberly Guilfoyle to resign, the White House said Tuesday, amid allegations that she sought money from a Trump supporter and accepted lavish hospitality from wealthy Greek businessmen. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>Former gang leader sentenced to 40 years to life for Tupac Shakur murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47befcfd84972679a50a87c103bf60f7e2fe5479039292ba30df27c00dc5c5e8</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T19:57:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-former-gang-leader-sentenced-to-40-years-to-life-for-tupac-shakur-murder--2d6357adbe6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-former-gang-leader-sentenced-to-40-years-to-life-for-tupac-shakur-murder" /><summary type="html">Duane “Keffe D” Davis, the former Los Angeles gang leader who boasted in books and interviews of his involvement in the killing of rapper Tupac Shakur, only to deny it when he came to trial, was sentenced to a minimum 40 years in prison on Tuesday.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>In Brazil, thousands march fearing return of Bolsonaro presidency</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:037886c05fe57e4bbdaa4ae7af37887f4c30a0a589e57901232b4c71771201aa</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T14:59:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/in-brazil-thousands-march-fearing-return-of-bolsonaro-presidency--752369db782e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/in-brazil-thousands-march-fearing-return-of-bolsonaro-presidency" /><summary type="html">Thousands of young Brazilians have taken to the streets to support President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and voice fears of a return to power for the Bolsonaro political movement, amid a closely watched presidential race. Many protesters say they are worried about their future, particularly the impact a far-right government could have on universities and education. FRANCE 24’s Jan Onoszko reports from Brazil.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump’s use of Russian diesel fuel, at Ukraine’s expense, sparks controversy in the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24f33430c8bf171bc474e6a3aef404756aa5c71fe3e2c242a5b2eb0a12201c4d</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T13:26:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-s-use-of-russian-diesel-fuel-at-ukraine-s-expense-sparks-controversy-in-the-us--8dd3eba1a3a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-s-use-of-russian-diesel-fuel-at-ukraine-s-expense-sparks-controversy-in-the-us" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump’s plan to import Russian diesel despite Western sanctions has sparked fierce criticism in Washington, including from Republicans, as high fuel prices and the upcoming midterm elections put pressure on his administration. His approach to the Ukraine war has also drawn controversy, with calls for Kyiv to hold elections and claims of an energy ceasefire announced without clear agreement from the parties involved. FRANCE 24's Douglas Herbert has the analysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>US economists win Nobel for research helping policymakers navigate crises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:679f29590c8f7d09153d6c29e521ea8ca044d7c492eb3b1bbe7f902931d56911</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T10:04:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-economists-win-nobel-for-research-helping-policymakers-navigate-crises--ba65e32638f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-economists-win-nobel-for-research-helping-policymakers-navigate-crises" /><summary type="html">Two American economists, Robert E. Hall of Stanford University and Michael Woodford of Columbia University, have won the Nobel Memorial Prize in Economic Sciences for their work on economic stabilisation. Their research helps policymakers and central banks better understand economic fluctuations, manage recessions and inflation, and account for public expectations when shaping economic policy. The prize money, worth around $1.2 million, will be shared equally between the two laureates.</summary></entry><entry><title>US immigration authorities raid home of Democratic Trump critic Ilhan Omar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b5baccd046b2c41b819b3b031383d4318e61b3cb151e4df782a9d4300a3d620</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T09:57:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-immigration-authorities-raid-home-of-democratic-trump-critic-ilhan-omar--1003e5999102.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-immigration-authorities-raid-home-of-democratic-trump-critic-ilhan-omar" /><summary type="html">US authorities raided the Washington home of Democratic Representative Ilhan Omar on Monday as part of an ongoing investigation into alleged immigration fraud, according to reports. The probe reportedly includes immigration paperwork completed by her late father when she was a child. Omar accused the Trump administration of using government institutions to target political opponents, describing the raid as an act of political intimidation. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson has the latest from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Breaking Bad' actor and disability activist RJ Mitte dies aged 34</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff551c27f14ff7b7d350019ff6697c11774747581ae4e3e51596dfe960083d40</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T01:43:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-breaking-bad-actor-and-disability-activist-rj-mitte-dies-aged-34--e0f5ef5dfa82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-breaking-bad-actor-and-disability-activist-rj-mitte-dies-aged-34" /><summary type="html">"Breaking Bad" actor RJ Mitte, who played Walter White Jr. in the hit US television series, has died aged 34, his representatives said Monday. The actor, who lived with cerebal palsy, also became a prominent disability rights advocate, championing inclusion and representation in film and television.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US federal agents raid home of Democratic congresswoman and Trump critic Ilhan Omar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e39c8d8f4b2fcdc13b2b73a79d941009b08ff6da3b3753e33cdae3e32987a283</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T15:13:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261012-us-federal-agents-raid-home-of-democratic-congresswoman-and-trump-critic-ilhan-omar--1078c3e6f713.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261012-us-federal-agents-raid-home-of-democratic-congresswoman-and-trump-critic-ilhan-omar" /><summary type="html">US federal agents on Monday launched a raid on ‌the Washington home of Democratic representative Ilhan Omar, an outspoken critic of US President Donald ⁠Trump, officials said. The raid followed a criminal fraud ‌investigation into the Somali-born lawmaker's immigration paperwork submitted by her late father when she ⁠was a child, Fox News reported.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Capital punishment in US: Elected judges, prosecutors seek 'results', 'not interested in the truth'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d7661bfa573c9e4744816b6ffdf38453ca4c628d506cbea2ffb5a56db865722</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T13:27:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261012-capital-punishment-in-us-elected-judges-prosecutors-seek-results-not-interested-in-the-trut--c9271d966485.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261012-capital-punishment-in-us-elected-judges-prosecutors-seek-results-not-interested-in-the-truth" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Sandrine Ageorges-Skinner, an advocate against the death penalty, author and member of the association "Ensemble contre la peine de mort" (Together Against the Death Penalty). She asserts that capital punishment is "really a political agenda, especially in electoral times."</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Inside Jeffrey Epstein's network: How favours, money and influence kept it running</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5208501bd4a91300448358ed14988d96523f261bc30a7025bbbd9bab97a60592</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T11:36:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261012-inside-jeffrey-epstein-s-network-how-favours-money-and-influence-kept-it-running--a47863837826.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261012-inside-jeffrey-epstein-s-network-how-favours-money-and-influence-kept-it-running" /><summary type="html">For years, convicted sexual predator Jeffrey Epstein developed a global web of powerful connections despite accusations of sex trafficking. Millions of declassified documents reveal how he expanded and maintainted his network.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula accuses social media giant Meta of election interference amid tight run-off campaign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3ab7d49a21b007b1c6018ade3f21fd87d58e52d9b049523443374df6bd44f84</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T13:12:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261011-brazil-lula-accuses-social-media-giant-meta-election-interference-amid-tight-run-campaign--d8ebedff7d11.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261011-brazil-lula-accuses-social-media-giant-meta-election-interference-amid-tight-run-campaign" /><summary type="html">Social media platform Meta has 48 hours to respond to claims by Brazil's leftwing candidate and incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's campaign accusing the tech platform of blocking content on the company's platforms. Brazil's Superior Electoral Court on Saturday gave the social media giant 48 hours to clarify whether it reduced the reach of posts by Lula's campaign ahead of the tight October 25 run-off against rightwing candidate Flavio Bolsonaro.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Convicted murderer Christa Pike leaves hospital, returns to prison after botched execution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0150032778a5757b2781e3c7f2af9d75e460519db77a383250624916a364055e</id><updated>2026-10-16T19:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T17:41:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261010-convicted-murderer-christa-pike-leaves-hospital-returns-to-prison-after-botched-execution--557dbe1b2584.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261010-convicted-murderer-christa-pike-leaves-hospital-returns-to-prison-after-botched-execution" /><summary type="html">Christa Pike's lawyers on Saturday said that the 50-year-old convicted murderer has been discharged from the hospital and returned to prison. Pike was transported to the hospital in critical condition on September 30 after she survived Tennessee's botched effort to execute her for murdering a classmate when she was a teenager.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
